    "type": "game",
    "name": "AnimSprite Pixelizer - Convert Hand-drawn Animations to Pixel Art",
    "steam_appid": 3849460,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>AnimSprite Pixelizer</strong> is a desktop application that optimizes the workflow for creating pixel animations for games, such as walking sprites.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849460/extras/a6a0a2c325a146033abd0a6c0b79caa9.poster.avif?t=1753101005\" width=640 height=386 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849460/extras/a6a0a2c325a146033abd0a6c0b79caa9.webm?t=1753101005\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849460/extras/a6a0a2c325a146033abd0a6c0b79caa9.mp4?t=1753101005\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It converts multiple frames with unified pixel settings, enabling efficient creation of consistent animation assets. Perfect for converting hand-drawn animations into game-ready pixel art.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849460/extras/1c3e4c916282fad3c7d881d149e604b0.avif?t=1753101005\" width=800 height=450 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can try the conversion quality with the free web version app in the Basic Information tab. This desktop app adds practical 2D game development features to the web version's conversion processing, including multi-frame support, animation preview, and sprite sheet output. Since it can export configuration files (.json), you can easily restore settings when re-converting modified artwork.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849460/extras/92e9c1e98895529b3b17a1acd3a024c7.avif?t=1753101005\" width=600 height=600 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849460/extras/51dea8b284e35dbea0cda59b2b71035f.avif?t=1753101005\" width=600 height=600 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83c\udfaf <strong>Recommended for:</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >2D Game Developers: Those who want to efficiently create animation sprites</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Indie Game Developers: Those who want to incorporate hand-drawn animations into games</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pixel Artists: Those who want to create multiple frames with unified quality</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u2728 <strong>Key Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Batch conversion of multiple frames (impossible with web version)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Animation preview in pixelized state (adjustable playback speed)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Automatic sprite sheet generation (up to 20 frames)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Consistent quality assurance (maintains consistency between frames)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Transparent PNG output</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f <strong>Technical Specifications</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Supported Formats</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Input: PNG, JPG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, WebP (all major image formats)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Output: PNG (transparent background support) + JSON configuration file</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Processing Capabilities</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Maximum canvas size: 1500\u00d71500px *Larger sizes are automatically resized</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pixel size range: 1-30px (finely adjustable according to usage)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sprite sheet: Fixed 5-column grid, supports up to 20 frames</p></li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>AnimSprite Pixelizer</strong> is a desktop application that optimizes the workflow for creating pixel animations for games, such as walking sprites.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849460/extras/a6a0a2c325a146033abd0a6c0b79caa9.poster.avif?t=1753101005\" width=640 height=386 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849460/extras/a6a0a2c325a146033abd0a6c0b79caa9.webm?t=1753101005\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849460/extras/a6a0a2c325a146033abd0a6c0b79caa9.mp4?t=1753101005\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It converts multiple frames with unified pixel settings, enabling efficient creation of consistent animation assets. Perfect for converting hand-drawn animations into game-ready pixel art.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849460/extras/1c3e4c916282fad3c7d881d149e604b0.avif?t=1753101005\" width=800 height=450 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can try the conversion quality with the free web version app in the Basic Information tab. This desktop app adds practical 2D game development features to the web version's conversion processing, including multi-frame support, animation preview, and sprite sheet output. Since it can export configuration files (.json), you can easily restore settings when re-converting modified artwork.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849460/extras/92e9c1e98895529b3b17a1acd3a024c7.avif?t=1753101005\" width=600 height=600 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849460/extras/51dea8b284e35dbea0cda59b2b71035f.avif?t=1753101005\" width=600 height=600 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83c\udfaf <strong>Recommended for:</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >2D Game Developers: Those who want to efficiently create animation sprites</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Indie Game Developers: Those who want to incorporate hand-drawn animations into games</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pixel Artists: Those who want to create multiple frames with unified quality</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u2728 <strong>Key Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Batch conversion of multiple frames (impossible with web version)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Animation preview in pixelized state (adjustable playback speed)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Automatic sprite sheet generation (up to 20 frames)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Consistent quality assurance (maintains consistency between frames)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Transparent PNG output</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f <strong>Technical Specifications</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Supported Formats</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Input: PNG, JPG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, WebP (all major image formats)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Output: PNG (transparent background support) + JSON configuration file</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Processing Capabilities</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Maximum canvas size: 1500\u00d71500px *Larger sizes are automatically resized</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pixel size range: 1-30px (finely adjustable according to usage)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sprite sheet: Fixed 5-column grid, supports up to 20 frames</p></li></ul>",
